cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use AeroMind in your research, please cite it using the metadata below.
  A BibTeX entry is also available in the README.
type: software
title: "AeroMind: Poisoning the Control Plane of LLM-Driven UAV Agents"
abstract: >-
  AeroMind is a multi-agent UAV autonomy research testbed demonstrating that shared
  persistent memory in LLM-driven systems constitutes an unguarded control plane.
  Three poisoned episodic records suffice to physically redirect both Scout UAVs
  across all seven evaluated planning backends, producing a consistent ~30 m deviation.
  The repository includes 15 attack scenarios, a three-layer retrieval-boundary defense,
  and complete reproducibility scripts for RAID 2026.
